      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{5}{3}\\cos^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)-\\frac{5}{3}\\sin^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{5}{3}\\left(\\cos^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=168^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 168^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(336^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{5}{3}\\left(\\cos^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(168^\\circ\\right)\\right)&=\\frac{5}{3}\\cos\\left(336^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
